.TH ODOO-REPORT-EDITOR 1 "October 2026" "QWeb Studio" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
odoo-report-editor \- edit Odoo QWeb reports with a live A4 preview
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B odoo-report-editor
.RI [ directory ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
QWeb Studio reads a local Docker Compose project and opens a report editor
in the browser. Select a model, report and sample record, edit the template,
and export an Odoo XML file. The current directory is used by default.
.PP
The editor listens on 127.0.0.1. A running Odoo service and its PostgreSQL
database are required unless demo mode is selected.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Use fictional data without Docker or Odoo.
.TP
.BI \-\-service " NAME"
Select the Odoo Compose service.
.TP
.BI "\-d, \-\-database " NAME
Select the Odoo database.
.TP
.BI "\-f, \-\-compose-file " FILE
Use an alternative Compose file.
.TP
.BI \-\-python " PATH"
Select the Python executable inside the Odoo container.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
Choose the local HTTP port. The default is 8765.
.TP
.B \-\-no-browser
Do not open the browser automatically.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command-line help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I report_editor_exports/
Exported XML files inside the selected project directory. Saving does not
overwrite module sources or stored Odoo template architectures.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
odoo-report-editor /path/to/odoo-project
odoo-report-editor --demo --port 8877
odoo-report-editor -d example --service odoo --no-browser
.fi
